            <ArticleTitle>Psilocybin-assisted therapy for <i>treatment-resistant</i> depression: a randomized, placebo-controlled trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <StartPage>2698811261234567</StartPage>
                <MedlinePgn>2698811261234567</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/02698811261234567</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Treatment-resistant depression (TRD) affects about one third of patients with major depressive disorder.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We randomly assigned 120 adults with TRD to psilocybin or an active placebo, each with psychological support. The primary outcome was the change in MADRS score at week&#xa0;6.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">MADRS scores fell more with psilocybin (difference &#x2212;7.4 points; 95% CI &#x2212;10.9 to &#x2212;3.9; <i>p</i> &lt; 0.001). Headache and nausea were the most common adverse events.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Psilocybin with psychological support reduced depressive symptoms over 6 weeks.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>&#xa9; The Author(s) 2026.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
